WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.172
Zann didn't have to think very hard about his decision.

2
00:00:03.173 --> 00:00:07.158
"Sorry," he told Venna. "I have to help my friend."

3
00:00:07.159 --> 00:00:11.368
"Let's go." Teplo sounded pleased. "I have a plan in mind."

4
00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:16.438
"You're making a mistake, Zann," Venna warned. "Magica needs you."

5
00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:20.164
"Gliss needs me too." Zann walked toward the door.

6
00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:25.944
Venna glanced at her assistants. Zann held his breath. Would she try to stop him?

7
00:00:25.945 --> 00:00:32.691
She didn't. Soon Zann, Perda, Darb, Zing, Teplo, and Fala were outside.

8
00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:35.763
"What's your plan?" Perda asked Teplo.

9
00:00:35.764 --> 00:00:42.498
The old man pulled a hat out of his cloak, jamming it over his red hair. He tossed another hat to Zann.

10
00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:46.240
"I'll tell you on the way to the zoo."

11
00:00:46.241 --> 00:00:52.008
"Your plan sounds crazy," Perda told Teplo. "Can it really work?"

12
00:00:52.009 --> 00:00:54.133
They had been walking for twenty minutes.

13
00:00:54.135 --> 00:01:00.959
"Of course." Teplo sounded confident. "I've known much crazier plans to work perfectly."

14
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:07.516
Fala looked dubious. "That's an awful lot of magic for one person—even a Magic Master.

15
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:10.031
Do you think you can handle it?"

16
00:01:10.032 --> 00:01:15.617
"I haven't used any magic in days," Teplo said. "I'm rested and ready."

17
00:01:15.618 --> 00:01:18.912
"Hush!" Darb whispered. "More trolls."

18
00:01:18.913 --> 00:01:22.480
They ducked into a doorway and waited for the trolls to pass.

19
00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:25.796
Every second felt like an hour to Zann.

20
00:01:25.797 --> 00:01:28.654
"Are we almost there?" he whispered.

21
00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:32.849
Fala nodded. "Follow me. I know a secret way in."

22
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.725
Soon they were pushing through a thick hedge.

23
00:01:35.726 --> 00:01:39.615
They peered out at the zoo, which was swarming with trolls.

24
00:01:39.616 --> 00:01:42.897
"The dragon pen is over there," Fala whispered.

25
00:01:42.898 --> 00:01:45.372
Zann had been to the zoo as a little kid.

26
00:01:45.373 --> 00:01:50.381
He remembered staring at the menacing wild dragons inside their iron-barred cage.

27
00:01:50.382 --> 00:01:55.005
Even knowing that the pen was a vacuum hadn't made the dragons less scary.

28
00:01:55.006 --> 00:02:00.537
Now the cage looked the same. But it was crammed full of people instead of dragons.

29
00:02:00.538 --> 00:02:03.025
"There's Gliss!" Darb whispered.

30
00:02:03.026 --> 00:02:06.003
Zann spotted their friend among the other prisoners.

31
00:02:06.004 --> 00:02:08.793
She was sitting on a rock, looking nervous.

32
00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:14.879
"It looks as if the trolls have captured every Red in First City!" Perda whispered.

33
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.089
"Not quite." Teplo stared past the pen. "Here comes one more."

34
00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.406
A troll carrying an elderly woman stomped toward the cage.

35
00:02:24.407 --> 00:02:29.020
Darb glanced at Fala. "You said they needed only one more prisoner."

36
00:02:29.021 --> 00:02:34.042
"There's no time to waste," Zann said. "Teplo's plan might not be perfect.

37
00:02:34.043 --> 00:02:37.589
But even a crazy plan is better than none, right?"

38
00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.477
Teplo grinned. "That's the spirit, my boy!

39
00:02:40.478 --> 00:02:44.176
Let's see if we can get closer while they're distracted."

40
00:02:44.177 --> 00:02:49.232
Most of the other trolls were watching the one troll try to wrestle the new Red into the pen.

41
00:02:49.233 --> 00:02:54.375
Teplo dashed across the open area beside the pen. Zann and the others followed.

42
00:02:54.376 --> 00:02:59.335
When they reached the shelter of some shrubs, Teplo started fishing around inside his cloak.

43
00:02:59.336 --> 00:03:04.472
"Are you sure you can manage all that magic at once?" Fala asked him.

44
00:03:04.473 --> 00:03:08.075
"It'll require a tremendous amount of energy."

45
00:03:08.076 --> 00:03:14.962
"I could help," Zann offered. "Combine my energy with yours, take some of the smaller spells . . ."

46
00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:17.692
"Thank you, Zann. But no," Teplo said.

47
00:03:17.693 --> 00:03:22.717
"You don't have the experience for this type of magic. Besides, it's far too risky."

48
00:03:22.718 --> 00:03:27.488
Teplo pulled a large, lumpy turnip out of his cloak and tossed it into the grass.

49
00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:31.320
By the time it settled near the dragon pen, he'd pulled out more.

50
00:03:31.321 --> 00:03:34.845
Soon dozens of turnips dotted the ground.

51
00:03:34.846 --> 00:03:38.203
The trolls had finished locking away the new prisoner by now.

52
00:03:38.204 --> 00:03:43.556
Most of them wandered away, grunting loudly at one another as if discussing what to do next.

53
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:47.834
The only troll that noticed the turnips was the one left guarding the prisoners.

54
00:03:47.835 --> 00:03:52.161
It stared at the vegetables with a look of dull confusion on its face.

55
00:03:52.162 --> 00:03:58.290
Teplo rubbed his hands together until sparks flew. "Animate," he murmured.

56
00:03:58.291 --> 00:04:01.827
The turnips started growing larger and larger.

57
00:04:01.828 --> 00:04:05.911
Then they changed shape, taking on human form.

58
00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:10.162
Within seconds they looked just like the Reds inside the pen!

59
00:04:10.163 --> 00:04:13.703
There was even one that looked exactly like Gliss.

60
00:04:13.704 --> 00:04:21.191
"Hurry," Fala hissed. "You have to hide the real prisoners, or they'll figure it out—even trolls aren't that dumb!"

61
00:04:21.192 --> 00:04:24.931
Teplo nodded. Beads of sweat dotted his face.

62
00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:30.835
But he rubbed his hands even harder and pointed at the pen. "Cloak," he muttered.

63
00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:35.832
Suddenly it was as if a sheer curtain had been dropped over the entire pen.

64
00:04:35.833 --> 00:04:40.175
The Cloaking spell dimmed the view of the prisoners but didn't hide them completely.

65
00:04:40.176 --> 00:04:44.027
"More!" Fala urged. "Let me help you!"

66
00:04:44.028 --> 00:04:47.322
"No—let me." Zann pushed past her.

67
00:04:47.323 --> 00:04:52.556
Grabbing Teplo's hands, he rubbed his own against them, joining their friction together.

68
00:04:52.557 --> 00:04:58.253
"Not . . . safe!" Teplo gasped, his face drenched in sweat.

69
00:04:58.254 --> 00:05:01.281
But he didn't pull away as Zann focused his energy.

70
00:05:01.282 --> 00:05:08.337
Zann was good at Cloaking spells; he used them frequently to play tricks on Zing. "Hide," he muttered.

71
00:05:08.338 --> 00:05:11.342
"It's working!" Perda whispered.

72
00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:16.405
Zann pulled his hands away. The Cloaking spell was complete.

73
00:05:16.406 --> 00:05:19.721
The pen appeared to be completely empty!

74
00:05:19.722 --> 00:05:23.930
At the same time, Teplo's turnip army started to move.

75
00:05:23.931 --> 00:05:27.643
The old man was still creating friction as fast as he could.

76
00:05:27.644 --> 00:05:30.938
As he did, the fake Reds started running around.

77
00:05:30.939 --> 00:05:34.176
The guard troll was still staring in amazement.

78
00:05:34.177 --> 00:05:37.778
"Isn't it going to warn the others?" Perda wondered.

79
00:05:37.779 --> 00:05:43.534
"Maybe in about an hour," Zann said, "when its brain catches up to its eyes."

80
00:05:43.535 --> 00:05:47.878
"We can't wait that long." Fala glanced anxiously at Teplo.

81
00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:51.829
He was groaning and sweating with effort. "You'd better do something."

82
00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:57.453
Teplo glanced at Zann. "Can you do a Sound-Shifting spell?" he asked.

83
00:05:57.454 --> 00:06:01.431
Zann gulped. He remembered studying that type of spell in school.

84
00:06:01.432 --> 00:06:04.489
But he hadn't been paying much attention that day.

85
00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:14.642
"Yes." Perda spoke up, holding out her hands to Zann. "He can. I'll help."

